592186221249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050681 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186221250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050681 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186221251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050681 #edb/ref 1031 "Properties of Lines Given in Standard or General Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050681 #edb/ref 1033 6412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050681 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5e8ff420-568f-59ab-ad75-0d845d527b09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051055 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186221282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051055 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186221283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051055 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186221284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051055 #edb/ref 1031 "The Relationship Between Systems of Linear Equations and Graphs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051055 #edb/ref 1033 6436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051055 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7d9735be-c6fa-5179-9870-6c07397ae6a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179474 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13979" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179474 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the slope of the line $4x-2y=1$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179474 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9b0cfd54-9310-59e6-91cb-5b18413ae7b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179474 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the slope of the line if we can express its equation in slope-intercept form. To do this, we solve for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 2y &= 1 \\\\\n- 2y &= -4x + 1 \\\\\n2y &= 4x - 1 \\\\\n\\frac{2y}{2} &= \\frac{4x - 1}{2} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4x}{2} - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\ny &= 2x - \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the slope-intercept equation, we can tell that the slope of the line is $m=2$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179475 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13982" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179475 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the point where the line $4x-3y=8$ intersects the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179475 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d1904d74-7f31-5211-b7d4-88f4f5042d64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179475 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $x$-intercept, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $x$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4x-3y&=8 \\\\[5pt] 4x-3(0)&=8 \\\\[5pt] 4x&=8 \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{4x}{4}&=\\dfrac{8}{4} \\\\[5pt] x&=2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $2$, and we conclude that the line intersects the $x$-axis at\n\n$$\n\\left(2,0\\right)\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179476 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13986" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179476 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the point where the line $5x -4y=-8$ intersects the $y$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179476 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cbfa4dda-a399-5450-bacd-7681aebceede" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179476 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation and solve for $y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - 4y &= -8 \\\\\n5(0) - 4y &= -8 \\\\\n- 4y &= -8 \\\\\ny &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $2$, and we conclude that the line intersects the $y$-axis at\n\n$$\n\\left(0,2\\right)\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179631 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179631 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179631 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179631 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179631 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Slope of a Line Given Standard Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179631 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179631 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "48f52c24-cd5a-5701-8ec2-1d833e87a25f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179632 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179632 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179632 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the X-Intercept of a Line" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179632 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 175921861794